//? Title: Gaussian elimination: actual row reduction and numerical limits
//? Subtitle: Partial pivoting, original-system evidence, element growth, backward error and safe owned histories
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given a square coefficient matrix and a right-hand side, find the unknowns that
satisfy their simultaneous linear equations. Floating-point row operations can
introduce rounding error, and some systems have no unique solution.
Gaussian elimination first reduces the system to a triangle, then substitutes
backwards. This report follows actual core snapshots on a two-equation example
and the original three-equation system. Measured work and a maximal-growth family
show what partial pivoting controls and what it cannot guarantee. Residuals,
absolute pivot cutoffs and history admission provide separate, explicit checks.
)

\toc

> A swap, one elimination, then back substitution

Start with x+y=3 and 2x+3y=8. The larger first-column coefficient is 2, so row 1
moves above row 0. Subtract half of the new first row from the second:
its equation becomes -0.5y=-1. Thus y=2, followed by x=(8-3y)/2=1.
The native trace records accepted pivot choices, completed row eliminations and
back-substitution assignments at their actual time. A pivot snapshot follows
its row interchange; it is not a separate swap event. IDs are zero-based.
Before substitution the solution vector is empty; during it, earlier unsolved
coordinates are zero placeholders.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gaussian_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/gaussian_elimination.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const auto t=dm::algorithms::gaussian_elimination_trace({{1,1},{2,3}},{3,8},73);
 std::print("| event | column | selected/updated row | pivot/factor/solution value | transformed RHS | solution state |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n");
 for(const auto&e:t.events)std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {:.3f} | {} | {} |\n",e.kind,e.column,e.row,e.value,e.rhs,e.x);
 std::print("\nSolution {}; row order {}; swaps {}; eliminations {}; retained entries {}; growth {:.1Lf}.\n",t.run.solution.x,t.run.row_order,t.run.work.row_swaps,t.run.work.eliminations,t.captured_entries,t.run.growth);
 const auto& pivot=t.events.at(0);const auto& eliminate=t.events.at(1);const auto& last=t.events.back();
 dm::graphics::Diagram d(65,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=4.4;box.height=2.25;box.font_size=21;
 d.node("pivot",{0,0},std::format("Swap row 0 with row {}\n{:.1f}x + {:.1f}y = {:.1f}\nrow order {}",pivot.row,pivot.matrix[0][0],pivot.matrix[0][1],pivot.rhs[0],pivot.row_order),box)
  .node("eliminate",{6,0},std::format("Subtract {:.1f} times row 0\n{:.1f}y = {:.1f}\nbelow-pivot entry {:.1f}",eliminate.value,eliminate.matrix[1][1],eliminate.rhs[1],eliminate.matrix[1][0]),box)
  .node("back",{12,0},std::format("Substitute backwards\ny = {:.1f}, then x = {:.1f}\nactual result {}",last.x[1],last.x[0],last.x),box)
  .edge("pivot","eliminate","row update").edge("eliminate","back","triangle")
  .text({6,2.4},"Actual partial pivoting and row reduction",27).save_svg("build/gaussian_tiny.svg");
 if(t.run.solution.x!=std::vector<double>{1,2}||t.events.size()!=5)throw std::runtime_error("tiny actual solve");
}
