\alttext(Two augmented matrices show the original rows and actual upper triangle. The reduced diagonal is about minus3,1.667,0.2 and the transformed RHS about minus11,4.333,minus0.2. Final original-row order is1,2,0.)

Printing six digits previously hid rounding: the computed second coordinate is
slightly above 3 and the third slightly above -1. The result is an approximation,
not an exact-arithmetic solution. The library preserves the actual pre-edit
execution, including its cancellation signs. The old cached report displayed a
minus sign on a zero that the unchanged program in this toolchain prints as plus.
Neither sign changes the represented equation or residual.

> Count the implemented work, including the cancelled entry

At column k, the implementation updates n-k coefficients in each of n-k-1 later
rows. It includes the entry being eliminated and does not overwrite a tiny
cancellation residue with a manufactured exact zero. For a successful solve:

$$
\begin{aligned}
C_{\rm rows}&=C_{\rm comparisons}=C_{\rm RHS}=C_{\rm back\ products}=n(n-1)/2,\\
C_{\rm coefficient\ updates}&=\sum_{q=1}^{n}q(q-1)=n(n-1)(n+1)/3,\\
C_{\rm back\ divisions}&=n.
\end{aligned}
$$
\alttext(A successful solve performs a triangular number of row updates, candidate comparisons, RHS updates and back-substitution products; coefficient updates grow cubically as n times n minus one times n plus one divided by three.)

One coefficient update is a multiply-subtract, not one floating-point operation.
These counters exclude validation, allocation, finite checks and snapshot copies.
The ordinary solve needs O(n³) arithmetic and O(n²) storage. A full trace stores
O(n²) states of O(n²) entries each, so its worst-case history and copying cost
are O(n⁴). The following plot measures counts, not elapsed time.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gaussian_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/gaussian_elimination.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 std::vector<double>x,updates,pairs,history;
 std::print("| n | pivot comparisons | row eliminations | coefficient updates | RHS updates | back products | back divisions | whole trace entries |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
 for(std::size_t n:std::array<std::size_t,7>{4,8,16,32,64,128,256}){
  const auto a=dm::algorithms::gaussian_elimination_growth_matrix(n);const auto s=dm::algorithms::gaussian_elimination_solve(a,std::vector<double>(n,1));const auto bound=dm::algorithms::gaussian_elimination_trace_entries(n);
  std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,s.work.pivot_comparisons,s.work.eliminations,s.work.coefficient_updates,s.work.rhs_updates,s.work.back_products,s.work.back_divisions,bound);
  x.push_back(std::log2(double(n)));updates.push_back(std::log2(double(s.work.coefficient_updates)));pairs.push_back(std::log2(double(s.work.eliminations)));history.push_back(std::log2(double(bound)));
  if(!s.solution.solved||s.work.coefficient_updates!=n*(n-1)*(n+1)/3)throw std::runtime_error("actual cubic work");
 }
 auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();plot.lines(x,pairs,"Row updates",{37,99,235},2).points(x,pairs,"",{37,99,235},4)
  .lines(x,updates,"Coefficient updates",{220,38,38},2).points(x,updates,"",{220,38,38},4)
  .lines(x,history,"Whole trace entries",{22,163,74},2).legend({"Row updates","Coefficient updates","Whole trace entries"},{{37,99,235},{220,38,38},{22,163,74}})
  .title("Measured ordinary work versus virtual whole-history admission").xlab("log2 matrix order").ylab("log2 actual work counts or virtual retained entries").y_limits(1,38).size(1100,540).save_svg("build/gaussian_work.svg");
}
