> Absolute cutoffs, invalid inputs and whole-history admission

The legacy Gaussian API keeps its original absolute pivot cutoff 1e-12.
A selected pivot strictly below it returns solved=false and an empty solution;
equality is accepted. This does not classify inconsistent versus underdetermined
systems, and a uniformly tiny but perfectly conditioned identity matrix also
fails. New solve/trace APIs expose an explicit positive finite absolute cutoff;
they do not silently change the meaning to a relative threshold.

All row lengths, RHS length and finite entries are checked before pivoting,
including entries beyond an early zero pivot. Nonfinite stored arithmetic throws.
These checks prevent malformed access and false success with NaN/Inf, while
leaving the limits of finite precision explicit.

History admission counts the entire conservative request before copying inputs
or allocating solver state. With E=n(n-1)/2+2n possible events, its bound is

$$
H(n)=n^2+2n+E(1+n^2+4n).
$$
\alttext(History admission counts the original matrix rows and cells plus RHS, then all possible events with one metadata record, matrix rows and cells, RHS, row permutation and up to n solution entries.)

Each event owns its matrix, RHS, permutation and solution state. Input rows/cells
and event matrix row records count too. Ordinary final output, work/root metadata,
working storage and allocator bytes are excluded: entries are not bytes or peak
RAM. The default cap is one million; zero disables only the optional cap, while
arithmetic and container limits remain. A failure cannot return a partial trace,
and caller inputs remain unchanged. Rejected pivots do not get an early-stop
quota discount. Shape/finite/control validation precedes admission.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gaussian_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/gaussian_elimination.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const dm::algorithms::GaussianMatrix tiny{{1e-13,0},{0,1e-13}};const std::vector<double>rhs{1e-13,2e-13};
 const auto rejected=dm::algorithms::gaussian_elimination_solve(tiny,rhs);const auto accepted=dm::algorithms::gaussian_elimination_solve(tiny,rhs,1e-15);
 std::print("| scaled identity | cutoff | accepted | solution |\n| --- | ---: | --- | --- |\n| A=1e-13 I | 1e-12 | {} | {} |\n| A=1e-13 I | 1e-15 | {} | {} |\n",rejected.solution.solved,rejected.solution.x,accepted.solution.solved,accepted.solution.x);
 dm::algorithms::GaussianMatrix a{{1,1},{2,3}};std::vector<double>b{3,8};bool denied=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::gaussian_elimination_trace(a,b,67);}catch(const std::length_error&){denied=true;}
 auto t=dm::algorithms::gaussian_elimination_trace(a,b,73);a[0].clear();b.clear();t.events[0].matrix[0][0]=99;
 const bool owned=t.input[0]==std::vector<double>{1,1}&&t.events[1].matrix[0][0]==2&&t.run.upper[0][0]==2;
 bool shape=false,finite=false,overflow=false,virtual_count=false;
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::gaussian_elimination_trace({{1,2},{3}},{1,2},1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){shape=true;}
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::gaussian_elimination_trace({{0,0},{0,std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN()}},{0,0},1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){finite=true;}
 const double m=std::numeric_limits<double>::max();try{(void)dm::algorithms::gaussian_elimination({{m,m},{-m,m}},{m,m});}catch(const std::overflow_error&){overflow=true;}
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::gaussian_elimination_trace_entries(std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max());}catch(const std::length_error&){virtual_count=true;}
 const auto empty=dm::algorithms::gaussian_elimination_trace({},{});
 std::print("\nHistory upper {}; observed {}; cap 67 rejected {}; cap 73 admitted true; independent owned copies {}.\n",dm::algorithms::gaussian_elimination_trace_entries(2),t.captured_entries,denied,owned);
 std::print("Checks: shape before quota {}; later NaN before early pivot/quota {}; finite arithmetic overflow {}; virtual count overflow {}.\n",shape,finite,overflow,virtual_count);
 std::print("Empty: solved {}; coordinates {}; events {}; retained {}; residual infinity {}.\n",empty.run.solution.solved,empty.run.solution.x.size(),empty.events.size(),empty.captured_entries,dm::algorithms::gaussian_residual_summary({}, {},{}).residual_inf);
 auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({73.,double(t.captured_entries),67.},{"Whole admission","Actual retained","Rejected cap"});plot.title("Admit the whole trace, even when observed history is smaller").xlab("Two-equation owned history").ylab("Retained-history entries, not bytes").y_limits(0,85).size(1100,520).save_svg("build/gaussian_controls.svg");
 if(!denied||!owned||!shape||!finite||!overflow||!virtual_count||rejected.solution.solved||accepted.solution.x!=std::vector<double>{1,2})throw std::runtime_error("domain and quota controls");
}
