\caption(The scale example changes acceptance without changing conditioning. The history cap 73 admits a trace that retains 67 entries; a cap equal to the observed 67 still rejects the conservative request.)
\alttext(Three bars show whole admission73, actual retained67 and a rejected cap 67. Computed controls verify changed-cutoff acceptance, independent snapshots, full validation, arithmetic overflow and empty input.)

The native solve now supplies the row-reduction evidence that previously needed
a second implementation in the report. Partial pivoting controls multipliers,
while growth, conditioning, residuals and an absolute cutoff answer different
questions. These exact generated systems expose those distinctions without an
external dataset or a timing claim.
